From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:25:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 058/110] Column block edits line up on lines with tabs

A column block pasted, typed or deleted across a tab character landed right
of the tab, so the rows no longer lined up. A tab cut by an edge of the block
is now replaced by spaces of the same width first, as part of the same undo
step, so text goes in and out at the same visual column on every line. A
copy gives the columns of such a tab inside the block as spaces and keeps
whole tabs, so tab-separated columns copy as tabs.

Limits: the highlight still shows a tab cut by the left edge as outside the
block, although a copy includes its covered columns as spaces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

